 Group for Nutrition Reflection and Investigation, which focuses on managing patients with diabetes and stress hyperglycemia.", "HYPERGLYCEMIA:Hyperglycemia is a medical condition characterized by an excessive amount of glucose in the blood. It is often seen in patients with diabetes and may require dietary intervention to manage blood sugar levels effectively. If left untreated, hyperglycemia can lead to severe complications, highlighting the importance of monitoring and controlling blood sugar levels in affected individuals.", "PANCREATICODUODENECTOMY:Pancreaticoduodenectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of the pancreas and duodenum, often requiring specialized nutritional support post-surgery.", "NUTRITION SUPPORT:Nutrition support refers to the provision of nutrients and nutritional therapy to patients who are unable to eat or absorb sufficient nutrients due to various medical conditions, such as acute pancreatitis. This support is essential for individuals who cannot meet their nutritional needs through normal eating, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for recovery and overall health.", "TAPIA MJ:Tapia MJ is a researcher who co-authored studies on the prevalence of diabetes and its management in parenteral nutrition.", "OCÓN J:Ocón J is a contributor to research on insulin therapy and metabolic control in patients on total parenteral nutrition.", "CABREJAS-GÓMEZ C:Cabrejas-Gómez C is part of the study group focusing on hyperglycemia in parenteral nutrition.", "BALLENTEROS-POMAR MD:Ballenteros-Pomar MD is a researcher involved in the study of diabetes management in parenteral nutrition.", "GONZALEZ INFANTINO CA:Gonzalez Infantino CA is an author who studied hyperglycemia and hypoalbuminemia as mortality factors in patients with enteral feeding.", "GONZÁLEZ CD:González CD is a researcher who contributed to studies on hyperglycemia in patients receiving enteral nutrition."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperat